  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\r\n\r\nSee https://bug1910599.bmoattachments.org/attachment.cgi?id=9416887, where the behavior is different depending on whether the svg is in the list of available images. This happen per spec:\r\n\r\nQuestions:\r\n\r\n * Per spec you should hit the second case (both promises resolve) on [this wpt](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/0a595a5048225b38c91ee9de0a39474c713897f9/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/decode/image-decode-path-changes.html#L36-L47), but Chromium doesn't somehow?\r\n\r\n * It seems very confusing that, depending on whether the load is sync, you might end up with a promise resolving successfully for an image that you didn't intend to request a decode for. Do we want to synchronously reject the decode promises whenever \"update the image data\" runs? I guess that might be a bit over-agressive?",
